"""A Level French (0745), Upper Sixth: Etude des Oeuvres Francaises au Programme, Etude des Oeuvres Francophones Africaines au Programme,
Dissertation Litteraire et Commentaire Compose (9 lessons).

Taught in English for Anglophone learners; examples, quotations of method and model answers are in French. The prescribed works are not named
in the blueprint. The Board's 2023 subject report (French section) names, for Paper 2 Literature: Baudelaire (poems), Marivaux (Les Fausses
Confidences), Cesaire (La Tragedie du roi Christophe), Victor Hugo (Le Dernier Jour d'un condamne), Nkoa Atenga (L'Enfant de la revolte muette)
and Francis Bebey (Le Fils d'Agatha Moudio). Plot, character and theme facts are given ONLY in outline, in the author's own words, for the works
the author knows well (Les Fausses Confidences, Le Dernier Jour d'un condamne, Les Fleurs du mal in general, La Tragedie du roi Christophe, Le Fils
d'Agatha Moudio in outline); for L'Enfant de la revolte muette only the characters and themes the report names are used, the rest is a study
framework. Students are always told to check facts against their own copy. All unseen passages, poems and model extracts are original and
invented. Report facts are paraphrased and no question is claimed to come from a past paper.
"""

from .dsl import *  # noqa: F403

COURSE = ("french", "upper-sixth")

M_FR = "Étude des Œuvres Françaises au Programme"
M_AF = "Étude des Œuvres Francophones Africaines au Programme"
M_DIS = "Dissertation Littéraire et Commentaire Composé"

OWNCOPY = ("**Use your own copy.** This lesson gives a method and a few well-known facts in our own words. Check every fact, name and "
           "page against your own copy of the text before you use it in an essay: editions and teachers' notes differ.")


def qz(question, right, wrongs, pos, explanation, hint="", title="Quick check"):
    """QUIZ helper: `wrongs` is a list of (text, why) pairs; the right answer is inserted at index `pos`."""
    choices = [w[0] for w in wrongs]
    feedback = [w[1] for w in wrongs]
    choices.insert(pos, right)
    feedback.insert(pos, "")
    return QUIZ(question, choices, pos, explanation, hint=hint, feedback=feedback, title=title)


