        PQ("Why should an essay about Le Dernier Jour d'un condamné write « le condamné » and not « Hugo » for the person who suffers?", "Because the suffering voice belongs to a fictional narrator, while Hugo is the author who made him up. If you write « Hugo souffre », you confuse the two, and your analysis of narration is wrong. You may say « Hugo choisit de ne pas révéler le crime » to speak of the author's choice, and « le condamné se souvient de sa fille » to speak of the character."),
